# The same board and the same audio as 2600-v32bis-9600t-mnp4, driven
# down the classic ladder with no V.8 at all.
#
# V.32 is from 1988 and V.8 from 1994, so a V.32 modem has to start up
# without one -- and this one could not.  V.32 had no rung in the
# fallback ladder, so offering it alongside anything else meant it was
# reachable only through a CM/JM exchange, and a call to a V.32 board
# that did not speak V.8 settled for V.22bis at a quarter of the speed.
# 5.4.1 has the calling modem, after the answer tone, transmit carrier
# state A and listen for one of two incoming tones at 600 and 3000 Hz;
# the ladder has that rung now, and the tone bank has the two bins it
# needs to hear it with.
#
# The far end's half of this recording is unchanged -- it is a real
# board's alternating pair, not a synthesised one -- so what is being
# tested is only whether this end finds its way into Figure 4 without
# being told to.  The trace goes OAnsEnding, OAfterAns, Starting32, and
# then the whole of 5.4.1 in order.
source:    recordings/20260907T233626-+15642442600.wav
seconds:   30.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis,v32,v22bis
v8:        no
mnp:       4
connect:   V32bis 9600
expect:    https://2600.network - Patton 3120 #1
expect:    uSerNaME:
tolerance: 0
